SupraLINUX review for KDE CLI Tools 6.7.5

Use unchanged signed KDE source and authenticated Ubuntu packaging. Preserve
epoch 4, two binary packages, original public CLI/compatibility links, docs,
translations, completion, KCM, X11 support and Su/WidgetsAddons helpers.
Use exact eligible Frameworks 6.30 providers and Ubuntu Qt 6.10.2+dfsg-7,
including its required matching GuiPrivate SDK. No Qt transition.

Enable the original filetypestest and kcm_smoketest; selected KCMUtils 6.30
provides --smoke-test. Declare kbuildsycoca6, update-mime-database, fonts and
private-bus prerequisites. Native tests use owned HOME/XDG directories,
offscreen rendering and a bounded private session with no activation service
directories; the system bus is unavailable. Original assertions remain.

A public Ubuntu Qt SDK client invokes the actual installed CLI. Against only
owned files it checks MIME extension/content/stdin detection, rendered SVG
pixels, KIO cat/copy/move and the original compatibility link. Typed private
D-Bus fixture interfaces receive four inhibition requests, observe the child
command and release of caller connections, and receive an actual broadcast
notification signal. No real desktop inhibition, notification, eject, helper
authorization or device access occurs. Its bus/process groups/runtime are
removed and original stdout/stderr retained.

Compile that client against original Ubuntu before candidate installation,
retain its hash, and rerun the unchanged binary after normal APT upgrade.
Require both exact candidate versions and unchanged Qt runtimes. Rebuild a
consumer with the installed SDK, verify CLI/helper/KCM/docs/link payload and
APT consistency. Local original Ubuntu mechanism passed all ten commands,
four inhibition calls, one broadcast and own-resource cleanup. Candidate
native tests, packaging, ABI/upgrade and KVM execution are still pending.

Real authorization, device eject, application/desktop launching, interactive
filetype editing and real Wayland/X11 sessions remain later desktop QA.

Packaging revision 4:6.7.5-0supralinux2 prepares a native CMake test launcher
after debhelper compat13 sets HOME and clears XDG variables. CMake>=3.29 is
required for TEST_LAUNCHER. BUILD_TESTING, BUILD_DOC and WITH_X11 remain ON;
all original native tests and assertions remain unchanged. The suite keeps
its closed private bus; the executable target owns a fresh HOME/XDG fixture.

The launcher invokes the real update-mime-database and kbuildsycoca6 with
the original arguments and propagates failure. Only successful calls wait:
5.1 seconds for the frozen Qt MIME recheck interval and 1.6 seconds for
KService6.30's 1500ms cache recheck. No fake helper, signal, clock, provider
patch, assertion waiver or persistent user MIME/config state is introduced.
The test helpers and launcher remain integration fixtures in debian/tests.
Original source, Qt, Frameworks predecessor identities, installed Ubuntu
functional client and separately rebuilt consumer checks remain unchanged.

Attempt1 clean compilation completed; dh_auto_test failed two native rows.
The AppStream process returned success but skipped validation before install.
No completed candidate binaries, lintian or installed package tests existed.
Preserve its source/log/host archives and original FAIL. Offline zero-NIC
KVM controls establish complete unchanged native test coverage separately;
fresh authoritative input preflight and clean package execution are required
before any candidate package certification or delivery.
